Save verified EDID profiles as /etc/vita-dock-edid/*.bin.
Save build profiles in $USERPATCHES_PATH/vita-dock-edid/.
The service matches manufacturer, product, and serial bytes.
The service restores a profile when its preferred resolution is absent.
Name tested custom timing profiles *.force.bin to replace a matching EDID regardless of available resolutions.
Save matching layout settings in /etc/vita-dock-displays.conf.
Save build layout settings as $USERPATCHES_PATH/vita-dock-displays.conf.
Run systemctl restart vita-dock-edid.service after changing profiles.
Remove profiles and reconnect the hub to undo the override.
